# Manual upstream-runtime reproducer, intentionally NOT a passing game test.
# Pinned runtime 4bdffa88b35a496ca0a856a9eb58486cf6e2029c on OpenBSD 8.0:
# inspect reports "expected 65 got -1" and returns Void for this nested value.
# No game modules or native bridge are loaded. Inspecting either list on its
# own succeeds; a tuple containing both lists triggers the buffer-size failure.
# Run from the pinned runtime directory with kc3s/kc3s --load <this file> --quit.
value = {[(S64) 1, (U32) 1, (Uw) 1], [0, 1, 2]}
rendered = inspect(value)
if type(rendered) != Str do
  puts("FAIL: runtime inspect should return Str for the nested typed lists")
  exit(1)
end
puts(rendered)
